        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4fe6d87574b94d2f97254b0b6f92eeb3",
      "statement": "A reversed-polarity incident at connector J7 on an earlier board revision caused real hardware damage to GPIO13 (multimedia output driver, hard-shorted) and GPIO17 (light, via a swapped 12V control signal); GPIO18 (pump) survived the same incident, no firmware workaround exists, and the current sensor_config.h pin assignments apply only to the replacement board revision.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/sensor_config.h#L237-L245",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a4a9908484da4f141075a7e30513061de08e9c2089fe4671ccdf020063bb995d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/memory-bank/progress.md#L52-L52",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7b8b06bf65f6ff73264b6efb71448b3db0f801da56c800f5c23eacbed6dc8faa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4f4956676c2e4d59ac4e8ad39a880806",
      "statement": "Display 5V power (GPIO7) uses a safety-critical polarity on the current board revision: HIGH drives an N-MOSFET pre-driver Q5 that in turn drives the P-MOSFET Q4, so HIGH=ON and LOW/Hi-Z=OFF, inverting the polarity of the original single-FET design where driving the pin HIGH caused a ~300mA through-current.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/CLAUDE.md#L14-L14",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3dac598e98080c36f9bada69187802da67b01d0813cdf683a428ed5cfe6315af:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/sensor_config.h#L257-L263",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:43d3bc1a62acd4f48c7a5664dc974582a5c7bda4b69875d2603037d8b9279222:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1d76f4a6ce6d4338b036da28292389ca",
      "statement": "At boot, app_main.c releases the GPIO7 RTC hold and sets it Hi-Z, forces GPIO13 to OUTPUT LOW, initializes deep-sleep/touch-wakeup handling, then immediately pulses the 12V relay ON and enables Display 5V before starting NVS, WiFi, HTTP, sensor tasks (analog, BME680/BSEC, HX711, INA226), BLE scanners, BNO055 (after a 1s settle delay), and finally the Display-link modem.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/sensorboard/main/app_main.c#L92-L100",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:022c1188a39dc939c621728534584e70cebaadd20b9ccacd8fec611193ab50f1:"
